# --- Rust build output ---------------------------------------------------
# `target/` is the only large directory this repository produces. Everything
# in it is reproducible from `Cargo.lock`, which *is* tracked, so a clone plus
# `cargo build` gets the same bytes.
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# --- Snapshot testing ----------------------------------------------------
# `insta` writes a `.snap.new` beside a snapshot that did not match, and a
# `.snap.orig` when it rewrites one. Both are the *proposal*, not the record:
# the record is the `.snap`, which is reviewed and committed. A `.snap.new`
# in a commit is a snapshot somebody blessed without reading.
*.snap.new
*.snap.orig

# --- Programs the compiler produces --------------------------------------
# `sciencec build` leaves an object file beside the source and links an
# executable. Both are output; the `.science` file is the source of truth.
# Scoped to the corpus and the scratch tree rather than global, so a genuinely
# committed binary elsewhere would still be visible.
#
# **The extension list was the whole rule and it had a hole the size of two
# of the three supported hosts.** `Session::executable_path` gives the output
# `.exe` on Windows and *no extension at all* on macOS and Linux, so a pattern
# per extension matches nothing on either — and `sciencec build examples/…`
# there leaves an executable that `git add -A` will happily commit. It did.
# The corpus is a closed set of `.science` files and one `README.md`, so the
# rule is inverted: ignore everything in `examples/`, then name what belongs.
examples/*
!examples/*.science
!examples/*.md
# What each example prints, pinned by `sciencec`'s `corpus_output` test so a
# miscompile that still exits 0 changes a tracked file.
!examples/*.stdout
!examples/*/
tests/**/*.exe
tests/**/*.obj
tests/**/*.o

# --- Agent worktrees -----------------------------------------------------
# `.claude/worktrees/` holds git worktrees a background agent works in. Each
# is a checkout of this repository, so adding one produces a gitlink to an
# "embedded git repository" that a clone cannot follow.
.claude/

# --- A vendored LLVM checkout --------------------------------------------
# `llvm-project/` is ~600 MB of clone and is not a dependency: this backend
# binds LLVM's C API through an `extern` block against the installed
# `LLVM-C.lib`, so nothing here is built from that tree. Ignored so that
# cloning it for reference cannot end up in a commit.
llvm-project/

# --- Editors and operating systems ---------------------------------------
# `/.vscode/` is anchored on purpose: `editors/vscode/` is this project's own
# extension and is tracked. An unanchored `.vscode/` would silently ignore it.
/.vscode/
/.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Local environment ---------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
